WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.737
-Tonight was the first round
of the second series

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.004
of Democratic
presidential debates.

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:07.373
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:12.178 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.280
Of course, just because
it was the Democrats' big night

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.549
doesn't mean Donald Trump
could stay out of the news.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.718
In fact, he's physically
incapable of it.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.720
I'm shocked he didn't
crash through the wall

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.656
of the debate stage
in his golf cart.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.225
Trump, as usual, spent the
morning screaming at the TV

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.194
all day on Twitter,
ranting about everything

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.062
from his racist attacks
on Baltimore

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.797
to trade to morning talk shows,

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:33.366
to a possible
infrastructure bill,

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:36.669
tweeting, "Do I hear the
beautiful word 'bipartisan'?"

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.205
I don't know. Do you?
Let's listen.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:43.175 line:0%
-In a few moments, I will sign
a bar-- bipartisan bill.

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:45.011
-Of course, a bar partisan

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:48.915
is someone who only votes
while drunk.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:53.686
[Slurring] "Okay, now, how
do I get out of this booth?"

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.488
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.458
[Normal voice] Also, how do you
mess up the word "bipartisan"?

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.760
It's, like, the most
popular word in politics.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.630
That's like messing up the word
"Congress" or "lawmakers."

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.033 line:0%
-Lawmarkers.
-Alright.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.002
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:12.138
Trump was also asked today
if his racist attacks

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.340
on Congressman Elijah Cummings
in Baltimore

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.176
were part of some sort of
calculated political strategy,

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:20.813
which is both clearly not true
and also doesn't matter.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:22.282
It's just who Trump is.

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:24.417
He's a racist.
It's how he sees the world.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.286
And when he was asked today
if it was

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:28.554
some sort of grand strategy,
he said this.

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:32.491 line:0%
-There's no strategy. I have no
strategy. There's zero strategy.

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:35.227
-That would be an accurate
Trump response

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:37.130
to literally any question.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.631
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.166
"Mr. Trump..."

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:42.301
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:44.303
"Mr. Trump,
when you stand up straight,

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:46.605
are you intentionally
puffing your chest out

00:01:46.605 --> 00:01:48.474
like an angry kangaroo?"

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:51.043
"I have no --
I stand like this --

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:54.080
I stand like this because
my bones are hollowed out

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.415
from the Diet Coke."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:59.719
In fact, today was a day of
seemingly accidental confessions

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.521
from Trump, because
he was also asked by reporters

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:04.757
about a bipartisan
election security bill

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.693
that Senator Majority Leader
Mitch McConnell is blocking.

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:09.295
Trump tried to defend McConnell

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:12.065
from accusations that
he's essentially aiding Russia,

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.633
but I don't think
Trump's comment was helpful.

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:19.738 line:0%
-Mitch McConnell is a man
that knows less about Russia

00:02:19.738 --> 00:02:22.742 line:0%
and Russian influence
than even Donald Trump,

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.877 line:0%
and I know nothing.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:29.081
-I agree!
I mean, this is a crazy day.

00:02:29.081 --> 00:02:32.218
And, again...

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:35.054
an answer that could work
for literally any question.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.455
After his presidency is over

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:38.924
and they haul him in on
obstruction-of-justice charges,

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:41.226
he's going to be sitting
in an interrogation room

00:02:41.226 --> 00:02:43.763
telling the cops,
"It was all Mike Pence's idea."

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.164 line:0%
-I know nothing.

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:46.932
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:49.936
-All of this is why whatever
you think of the Democrats,

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.470
it was a relief
and a change of pace

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:52.938
to at least
hear a bunch of people

00:02:52.938 --> 00:02:56.509
who can speak in coherent
sentences about actual policies.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:59.312
The only time Elizabeth Warren's
ever been a bar partisan

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:03.549
is when she drank a beer
that one time on Instagram Live.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:05.685
Now, Warren was one of
the leading contenders

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.853
coming into tonight's debate,

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.855
along with her
close ideological ally

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.422
and longtime friend
Bernie Sanders.

00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:11.891
And coming
into the debate tonight,

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:12.992
there were a lot of questions

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.894
about how they'd handle
their friendship.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.696
The media couldn't help
but speculate.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:19.732
Would they go after each other,
or would they team up

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.334
to go after the moderates
onstage?

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.635 line:0%
-Tonight, the front-runners
in the center of the stage

00:03:23.635 --> 00:03:25.838 line:0%
are going to be Bernie Sanders
and Elizabeth Warren.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.840 line:0%
And one of the big questions
is, they're political allies.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.275 line:0%
Will they go after each other?
-They kind of seem

00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:33.146 line:0%
to have a pact that they
won't go after each other.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.481 line:0%
Does that pact
live through the evening?

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:38.217 line:0%
-They are seen as competing
for some of the same voters,

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:41.053 line:0%
so does she try to create
some differentiation

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:44.790 line:0%
with Senator Sanders,
or does she focus on Joe Biden

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.325 line:0%
or do a different thing?

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:48.795 line:0%
-I think Sanders and Warren
are more likely to team up

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:51.998 line:0%
against some of the more
moderate candidates onstage.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:54.333
-That's right. They should team
up. Like a wrestling duo.

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.603
Warren could start by giving
a lengthy explanation

00:03:56.603 --> 00:04:00.206
for her plans for a wealth tax
on assets over $50 million,

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:02.008
and then Bernie could tag in
and hit a billionaire

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:04.343
over the head with a chair!

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:06.946
And then there was
the rest of the field.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:09.015
Everyone was looking
for their moment to stand out.

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.850
And there were big questions
for each of them,

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.786 line:0%
questions like --
who the hell are these guys?"

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.855 line:0%
Would Beto bust out
his Spanish again?

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.924 line:0%
And since Cory Booker
wasn't onstage,

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:21.460 line:0%
would he make this face at home?

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:24.463 line:0%
Would Tim Ryan get caught
touring the debate stage again

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:28.301 line:0%
looking like a pledge
from Sigma Kai?

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:31.070 line:0%
And would Marianne Williamson
explode into

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:35.207 line:0%
a thousand butterflies
that spell out the word "love"?

00:04:35.207 --> 00:04:37.509
And then once the debate got
started, CNN chose to have

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:40.013 line:0%
the candidates come onstage
individually for intros

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:43.849 line:0%
like they were the original
"Star Trek" cast at Comic-Con.

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:46.519
And while some candidates
obviously had big fan bases,

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.921
others got more muted reactions.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.057 line:0%
-Senator Bernie Sanders.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:54.092 line:0%
[ Loud cheers and applause ]

00:04:54.092 --> 00:04:56.329 line:0%
Senator Elizabeth Warren.

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:59.464 line:0%
[ Loud cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.464 --> 00:05:01.267 line:0%
Mayor Pete Buttigieg.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:04.404 line:0%
[ Loud cheers and applause ]

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:06.906 line:0%
Former Congressman John Delaney.

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:10.176 line:0%
-Hi.
[ Subdued cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:12.011
-Oh, man, what a bummer
for that guy

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.747
to have to follow Warren,
Buttigieg, and Bernie.

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:17.549
It's like if Springsteen, Bono,
and the Rolling Stones

00:05:17.549 --> 00:05:18.984
all opened a concert,

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:22.888
and then they were followed
by a Weezer cover band.

00:05:22.888 --> 00:05:24.490
"Hey,
how you guys doin' tonight?

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.792
Hey, one more time
for Mick Jagger."

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:28.594
CNN spent
what seemed like an eternity

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:30.730
going through the rigmarole
of all the intros,

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.498 line:0%
the color guard,
the national anthem.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.834 line:0%
And then after all that,
Elizabeth Warren

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:38.737
returned the opening kickoff
for a 99-yard touchdown.

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:40.005
And then there was still more,

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:41.774
because they also
had opening statements.

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:43.542
We didn't even
get to our first question

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:44.910
until about 25 minutes in.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.413
You could've just watched
an entire episode of "Veep."

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.916
In fact, I'm pretty sure
anyone on "Veep" would've had

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:51.917
a better chance of getting
elected than this guy.

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:54.787
I mean, what --
what is this guy doing here?

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:57.290
And where's Gromit?

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.326
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:02.061
Of course...

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:03.829
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:06.231
We did get the benefit
of an opening statement

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:08.401
from Marianne Williamson,
who, right off the bat,

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:10.269
made it weird
with her word choice.

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:13.572 line:0%
-In 1776, our founders
brought forth on this planet

00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:15.808 line:0%
an extraordinary
new possibility.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:18.978
-On THIS planet?

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:21.047
"To be clear,
on the planet I'm from,

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:23.249
you can only vote if you've
gathered enough moon crystals

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:25.184
to please the ancient oracle."

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:27.320
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.855
And then the Democrats
immediately got into it,

00:06:29.855 --> 00:06:32.224
with the moderators
asking Bernie to respond

00:06:32.224 --> 00:06:34.994
to former Congressman
John Delaney's criticisms

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.662
of his Medicare for All plan.

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:39.365 line:0%
-You support Medicare for All,
which would eventually

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:41.067 line:0%
take private
health insurance away

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.868 line:0%
from more than 150 million
Americans

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:46.071 line:0%
in exchange for
government-sponsored healthcare

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:47.773 line:0%
for everyone.

00:06:47.773 --> 00:06:50.676 line:0%
Congressman Delaney just
referred to it as bad policy,

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:52.778 line:0%
and, previously,
he has called the idea

00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:56.582 line:0%
political suicide that will just
get President Trump re-elected.

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:59.018 line:0%
What do you say
to Congressman Delaney?

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:00.786 line:0%
-You're wrong.

00:07:00.786 --> 00:07:04.223 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:06.892
-Such a quick answer.
Bernie said that

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:09.561
like he's definitely
used those words before.

00:07:09.561 --> 00:07:11.430
"Sir, you ordered
the lobster bisque."

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:14.233
"You're wrong!
I ordered the chicken soup!

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:17.803
And I want those crackers!
Crackers for all!"

00:07:17.803 --> 00:07:20.939
And then,
after Delaney and others

00:07:20.939 --> 00:07:22.508
accused Bernie and Warren

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:24.610
of trying to make private
health insurance illegal,

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:27.012
Warren stepped in
to stop the bickering.

00:07:27.012 --> 00:07:29.648 line:0%
-Let's be clear about this.
We are the Democrats.

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:33.085 line:0%
We are not about trying to take
away healthcare from anyone.

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:35.821 line:0%
That's what the Republicans
are trying to do.

00:07:35.821 --> 00:07:40.626 line:0%
And we should stop using
Republican talking points

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:42.694 line:0%
in order to talk with each other

00:07:42.694 --> 00:07:45.765 line:0%
about how to best provide
that healthcare.

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:49.068
-Elizabeth Warren will
turn this car around right now,

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:51.370
and nobody's going
to Disneyland!

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.940
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.208
Bernie and Warren
had standout moments,

00:07:56.208 --> 00:07:58.777
and Bernie seemed
especially feisty early on.

00:07:58.777 --> 00:08:00.579
He was shouting over
the moderators

00:08:00.579 --> 00:08:01.680
when they interrupted him,

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:04.082
taking on the moderates
like Delaney,

00:08:04.082 --> 00:08:06.519
and landing a big blow
against Congressman Tim Ryan.

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:07.819 line:0%
-Senator Warren, it's your turn.

00:08:07.819 --> 00:08:09.722 line:0%
-Oh, can I complete that,
please?

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:11.090 line:0%
-Your time is up.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.659 line:0%
-They will be advertising
tonight with that talking point.

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:15.794 line:0%
Under Medicare for All,

00:08:15.794 --> 00:08:19.398 line:0%
the hospitals will save
substantial sums of money

00:08:19.398 --> 00:08:22.401 line:0%
because they're not going to be
spending a fortune doing billing

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:25.104 line:0%
and the other bureaucratic
things they have to do today.

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:26.672 line:0%
-I've done the math.
It doesn't add up.

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:28.640 line:0%
-Maybe you did that and
made money off of healthcare,

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:31.777 line:0%
but our job is to run
a nonprofit healthcare system.

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:33.879 line:0%
Medicare for All
is comprehensive.

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:37.316 line:0%
It covers all healthcare needs
for senior citizens.

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:38.584 line:0%
It will finally include

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:41.153 line:0%
dental care, hearing aids,
and eyeglasses.

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:42.688 line:0%
-But you don't know that.
-Second of all --

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:43.889 line:0%
-You don't know that, Bernie.
-Second of all --

00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:45.157 line:0%
-We'll come to you
in a second, Congressman.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:46.625 line:0%
-I do know it.
I wrote the damn bill.

00:08:46.625 --> 00:08:48.794 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:51.730
-Damn. Tim Ryan better hope
Medicare for All passes

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.932
'cause he's going to need
some healthcare for that burn.

00:08:53.932 --> 00:08:55.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:55.567 --> 00:08:58.671
Bernie scared him so bad,
Ryan turned white as a sheet

00:08:58.671 --> 00:09:01.106
40 years ago.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.106 --> 00:09:05.011
Tim Ryan got owned so hard,
his hat flew back onto his head.

00:09:05.011 --> 00:09:06.511
[ Laughter ]

00:09:06.511 --> 00:09:08.180
You know Bernie was waiting
for that moment.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:11.717
To be challenged on a bill you
wrote is a politician's dream.

00:09:11.717 --> 00:09:13.685
It's like if J.K. Rowling
was on "Jeopardy!"

00:09:13.685 --> 00:09:15.821
and one of the categories
was Boy Wizards.

00:09:15.821 --> 00:09:17.590
[ Laughter ]

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:19.158
But it seemed like
all the moderates

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:20.793
wanted a shot
at Warren or Bernie tonight.

00:09:20.793 --> 00:09:23.162
At one point, they debated
the question of whether

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:25.264
a self-described democratic
socialist like Bernie

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:26.532
could take on Trump,

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:28.667
and former Colorado Governor
John Hickenlooper

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:31.136
even tried to mock
Bernie's mannerisms,

00:09:31.136 --> 00:09:32.971
which only encouraged Bernie.

00:09:32.971 --> 00:09:36.342 line:0%
-So, again, I think,
if we're gonna force Americans

00:09:36.342 --> 00:09:37.877 line:0%
to make these radical changes,

00:09:37.877 --> 00:09:39.078 line:0%
they're not gonna go along.

00:09:39.078 --> 00:09:41.146 line:0%
You --
Throw your hands up, but you --

00:09:41.146 --> 00:09:42.548 line:0%
-Alright.
-You haven't --

00:09:42.548 --> 00:09:44.583 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oho! I can do it!

00:09:44.583 --> 00:09:46.985
-I feel like that's
the first and only time

00:09:46.985 --> 00:09:49.087
John Hickenlooper has said,
"Throw your hands up!"

00:09:49.087 --> 00:09:50.255
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:50.255 --> 00:09:53.825
And don't challenge Bernie
to pull a Bernie.

00:09:53.825 --> 00:09:55.027
"Oh, and let me guess --

00:09:55.027 --> 00:09:56.128
you're gonna do that thing
with your finger."

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:57.229
"Okay, I will do it,

00:09:57.229 --> 00:09:58.798
and I'm gonna point it
right at you!"

00:09:58.798 --> 00:10:00.132
[ Laughter ]

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:01.834
And then, when the moderates

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.635
kept challenging Warren
on her plans,

00:10:03.635 --> 00:10:05.071
claiming her ideas
were either impossible

00:10:05.071 --> 00:10:06.371
or politically impractical,

00:10:06.371 --> 00:10:08.908
she delivered what seemed
like a thesis statement

00:10:08.908 --> 00:10:10.876
for her candidacy
and for the night.

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:12.043 line:0%
-You know, I don't understand

00:10:12.043 --> 00:10:13.812 line:0%
why anybody goes
to all the trouble

00:10:13.812 --> 00:10:16.148 line:0%
of running for President
of the United States

00:10:16.148 --> 00:10:18.150 line:0%
just to talk about
what we really can't do

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.952 line:0%
and shouldn't fight for.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:20.952 --> 00:10:22.754
-Yeah, I mean, what's the point
of running for president

00:10:22.754 --> 00:10:24.757
if all your positions
are about stuff you can't do?

00:10:24.757 --> 00:10:26.826
It's like
if Ronald Reagan had said,

00:10:26.826 --> 00:10:30.129
"Mr. Gorbachev, make this wall
a little shorter."

00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:32.098
[ Light laughter ]

00:10:32.098 --> 00:10:33.299
Yeah.

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:35.667
[ Laughter ]

00:10:35.667 --> 00:10:38.503
[ Chuckles ]
[ Applause ]

00:10:38.503 --> 00:10:41.040
One of the --
One of the flash points --

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.675
One of the flash points
in this divide

00:10:43.675 --> 00:10:45.143
between the progressives
and the moderates

00:10:45.143 --> 00:10:46.445
was the climate crisis --

00:10:46.445 --> 00:10:47.979
the candidates disagreed over

00:10:47.979 --> 00:10:50.316
ambitious proposals
like the Green New Deal,

00:10:50.316 --> 00:10:52.551
and, again,
Ryan tried to take on Bernie.

00:10:52.551 --> 00:10:56.254 line:0%
-What do you do with an industry
that knowingly,

00:10:56.254 --> 00:10:59.725 line:0%
for billions of dollars
in short-term profits,

00:10:59.725 --> 00:11:02.227 line:0%
is destroying this planet?

00:11:02.227 --> 00:11:04.664 line:0%
I say that is criminal activity.
-Thank you.

00:11:04.664 --> 00:11:06.064 line:0%
-That cannot be allowed
to continue.

00:11:06.064 --> 00:11:08.100 line:0%
-Thank you, Senator Sanders.
Congressman, your response?

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.002 line:0%
-Well, yeah, I would --
I would just say --

00:11:10.002 --> 00:11:12.504 line:0%
I didn't say we couldn't
get there till 2040, Bernie.

00:11:12.504 --> 00:11:13.873 line:0%
You don't have to yell.

00:11:13.873 --> 00:11:17.009
-Oh, no, he --
he absolutely does have to yell.

00:11:17.009 --> 00:11:18.544
[ Laughter ]

00:11:18.544 --> 00:11:21.914
Bernie's been kicked out
of every library in Vermont.

00:11:21.914 --> 00:11:24.549
[ Laughter ]
He's like the bus from "Speed."

00:11:24.549 --> 00:11:28.219
If he goes under 100 decibels,
his hair will explode.

00:11:28.219 --> 00:11:30.422
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:30.422 --> 00:11:32.558
This debate basically seemed
like a bunch of moderates

00:11:32.558 --> 00:11:34.126
trying to take on
Warren and Bernie

00:11:34.126 --> 00:11:36.128
and Warren and Bernie teaming up
to fend them off.

00:11:36.128 --> 00:11:38.330
It like watching Michael Jordan
and Scottie Pippen

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:39.664
take on the Washington Generals.

00:11:39.664 --> 00:11:40.999
In fact, at one point,

00:11:40.999 --> 00:11:43.269
John Delaney was again called on
to debate Warren

00:11:43.269 --> 00:11:45.471
over her proposal
to impose a wealth tax

00:11:45.471 --> 00:11:47.472
on assets over $50 million,

00:11:47.472 --> 00:11:49.608
and she managed
to debate Delaney

00:11:49.608 --> 00:11:51.310
just with
her facial expressions.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.011 line:0%
-We can raise
the capital gains rate

00:11:53.011 --> 00:11:54.413 line:0%
to match the ordinary income.

00:11:54.413 --> 00:11:55.915 line:0%
You know,
the last president to do that

00:11:55.915 --> 00:11:57.216 line:0%
was actually Ronald Reagan.

00:11:57.216 --> 00:11:59.151 line:0%
We can do that
in our first year.

00:11:59.151 --> 00:12:00.319 line:0%
I've called for that to be done,

00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:02.487 line:0%
and it'll double
the earned income tax credit.

00:12:02.487 --> 00:12:05.457 line:0%
I called for the expansion
of universal pre-K,

00:12:05.457 --> 00:12:08.093 line:0%
so that every American
has pre-K.

00:12:08.093 --> 00:12:09.628
-[ Chuckling ] Damn.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:09.628 --> 00:12:11.396
Even when she's not talking,
she's winning.

00:12:11.396 --> 00:12:13.799
It's like when you're on the
subway next to the crazy guy

00:12:13.799 --> 00:12:15.166
and you try to signal
to your friend

00:12:15.166 --> 00:12:16.969
you want to move
without talking.

00:12:16.969 --> 00:12:19.271
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.271 --> 00:12:21.040
[ Mouthing words ]

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.508
[ Laughter ]

00:12:22.508 --> 00:12:24.843
Also, look
at how she rubs her hands

00:12:24.843 --> 00:12:26.645
when the wealth tax comes up.

00:12:26.645 --> 00:12:30.783 line:0%
-Your estimated net worth
is more than $65 million.

00:12:30.783 --> 00:12:31.983 line:0%
That would make you subject

00:12:31.983 --> 00:12:33.519 line:0%
to Senator Warren's
proposed wealth tax

00:12:33.519 --> 00:12:37.655 line:0%
on the assets of the richest
75,000 homes, households, or so

00:12:37.655 --> 00:12:39.158 line:0%
in the United States.

00:12:39.158 --> 00:12:40.626
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:40.626 --> 00:12:43.095
-[ Chuckles ]

00:12:43.095 --> 00:12:45.664
I mean, she was like
J.K. Rowling

00:12:45.664 --> 00:12:48.900
if the "Final Jeopardy!"
category was Boy Wizards.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:50.336
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:50.336 --> 00:12:52.771
And then, of course, there was
Marianne Williamson, again,

00:12:52.771 --> 00:12:54.840
who gave this answer
on the Flint water crisis.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:57.343 line:0%
-Flint is just the tip
of the iceberg.

00:12:57.343 --> 00:12:59.211 line:0%
I was recently
in Denmark, South Carolina,

00:12:59.211 --> 00:13:01.179 line:0%
where it is --
there is a lot of talk

00:13:01.179 --> 00:13:03.148 line:0%
about it being the next Flint.

00:13:03.148 --> 00:13:06.551 line:0%
We have an administration that
has gutted the Clean Water Act.

00:13:06.551 --> 00:13:07.920 line:0%
We have communities,

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:09.521 line:0%
particularly
communities of color

00:13:09.521 --> 00:13:12.024 line:0%
and disadvantaged communities
all over this country

00:13:12.024 --> 00:13:14.693 line:0%
who are suffering
from environmental injustice.

00:13:14.693 --> 00:13:16.395 line:0%
I assure you --
I lived in Grosse Pointe.

00:13:16.395 --> 00:13:18.997 line:0%
What happened in Flint would not
have happened in Grosse Pointe.

00:13:18.997 --> 00:13:21.300 line:0%
This is part
of the dark underbelly

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.034 line:0%
of American society.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:23.034 --> 00:13:26.705
-Wait. Was that good?
[ Laughter ]

00:13:26.705 --> 00:13:28.741
Is Marianne Williamson
like one of those albums

00:13:28.741 --> 00:13:30.075
you have to listen to
a couple of times

00:13:30.075 --> 00:13:31.910
before you figure out
what they were trying to do?

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:33.245
[ Laughter ]

00:13:33.245 --> 00:13:35.647
Is Marianne Williamson jazz?

00:13:35.647 --> 00:13:36.848
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:36.848 --> 00:13:38.383
Let's hear some more.

00:13:38.383 --> 00:13:41.086 line:0%
-You can't fight dog whistles --
you have to override them.

00:13:41.086 --> 00:13:42.421 line:0%
And the only way
you can override them

00:13:42.421 --> 00:13:44.757 line:0%
is with new voices,
voices of energy

00:13:44.757 --> 00:13:46.424 line:0%
that only come from the fact

00:13:46.424 --> 00:13:49.962 line:0%
that America has been willing
to live up to our own mistakes,

00:13:49.962 --> 00:13:51.863 line:0%
atone for our own mistakes,

00:13:51.863 --> 00:13:53.699 line:0%
make amends
for our own mistakes,

00:13:53.699 --> 00:13:56.368 line:0%
love each other,
love our democracy,

00:13:56.368 --> 00:13:58.003 line:0%
love future generations.

00:13:58.003 --> 00:14:00.139
-Okay. I think I'm gonna
put this album away.

00:14:00.139 --> 00:14:02.341
[ Laughter ]

00:14:02.341 --> 00:14:06.578
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:06.578 --> 00:14:09.114
But there were a couple things
that were a little odd

00:14:09.114 --> 00:14:10.715
about how this debate
was conducted.

00:14:10.715 --> 00:14:13.118
For one thing, they kept giving
so much time to John Delaney,

00:14:13.118 --> 00:14:15.354
a guy who's polling
at less than 1%.

00:14:15.354 --> 00:14:16.688 line:0%
-Congressman Delaney.
Congressman Delaney.

00:14:16.688 --> 00:14:17.923 line:0%
Congressman Delaney.

00:14:17.923 --> 00:14:19.124 line:0%
Congressman Delaney,
your response?

00:14:19.124 --> 00:14:20.860 line:0%
-Congressman Delaney,
I'll start with you.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.260 line:0%
-Congressman Delaney,
your response?

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:23.429 line:0%
Congressman Delaney.

00:14:23.429 --> 00:14:25.397 line:0%
Congressman Delaney,
I'm coming to you now.

00:14:25.397 --> 00:14:27.299
-Why do they keep asking him
to chime in?

00:14:27.299 --> 00:14:29.134
He's polling
within the margin of error.

00:14:29.134 --> 00:14:30.502
He's not gonna win.
[ Laughter ]

00:14:30.502 --> 00:14:32.538
It's like going
to a Maroon 5 concert

00:14:32.538 --> 00:14:34.873
if Adam Levine kept going,
"Alright!

00:14:34.873 --> 00:14:37.709
Now time for another drum solo!"
[ Laughter ]

00:14:37.709 --> 00:14:39.611
And Delaney
wasn't the only also-ran

00:14:39.611 --> 00:14:41.380
who got more stage time
than he probably should have --

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:43.314
there was also Tim Ryan,
who, for some reason,

00:14:43.314 --> 00:14:45.784
always seemed surprised
when they'd toss him a question.

00:14:45.784 --> 00:14:47.653 line:0%
-I want to go
to Congressman Ryan,

00:14:47.653 --> 00:14:51.090 line:0%
and I want to turn
to the subject of North Korea.

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:53.592
-I mean, my goodness -- he
looked like a long-haul trucker

00:14:53.592 --> 00:14:55.461
desperately fighting
to stay awake.

00:14:55.461 --> 00:14:56.862
[ Laughter ]

00:14:56.862 --> 00:15:00.699
"130 miles to Tulsa.
Maybe if I take off one shoe..."

00:15:00.699 --> 00:15:02.700
[ Laughter ]

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:04.937
[ Laughter continues ]

00:15:04.937 --> 00:15:08.306
Ultimately, this was
a deeply substantive debate

00:15:08.306 --> 00:15:11.042
that showcased genuine
differences among the candidates

00:15:11.042 --> 00:15:12.477
on key policy questions.

00:15:12.477 --> 00:15:14.179
And no matter what you think
of any them,

00:15:14.179 --> 00:15:16.982
eventually, one of them's
gonna go up against a guy

00:15:16.982 --> 00:15:19.151
whose campaign slogan
is basically...

00:15:19.151 --> 00:15:20.519 line:0%
-I know nothing.

00:15:20.519 --> 00:15:22.521
[ Laughter ]
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:22.521 --> 00:15:25.724 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

